I'm a little late in the discussion, but unless I've missed it,
no one has pointed out the obvious intrinsic for a can of
jumping beans: jumping!

Re: this definition.
I don't really like how the contents/nutrition of the tin change
with BUC status. If I eat one tin of a pair and get
string beans, it seems somewhat phony to bless the second
one to transubstantiate it into jumping beans. I think having
X% of all bean tins being jumping beans would be better, with
effects depending on BUC status. For example: B gives permanent
teleportitis, U gives teleportitis for a time (or maybe until
you eat again?), C ports you uncontrolled and you lose
intrinsic teleportitis if you had it.

One way to minimize the benefit to vegans would be to have
the tins of beans sometimes be generated in place of a tin of
a well-chosen vegan corpse. For example, brown molds. So
rather than gaining a free shot at an intrinsic a vegan is giving
up a chance at another (if more available) intrinsic.

Another way to give them a different occurance profile would
be to never generate them on the ground, but only in the
inventories of soldiers in place of a C or K ration (at some
probability).

